ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Eval harness maintainers and researchers running maj@k self-consistency on symbolic-answer math benchmarks (MATH, competition math) where answer surface forms vary (fractions, radicals, pi). Also model teams comparing models with different output verbosity. Need arises when choosing canonicalizer recall: high-recall numeric normalizers (Minerva-style) can merge true equivalents, but on phi<<0 datasets this hurts accuracy and can flip rankings.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Real win, not microbench-only, for the ecological foothold; microbench-only for the headline inversion. q=1.0000 on GSM8K and MATH-500 with zero adversarial false-merges (results/precision_recall.csv) proves real numeric graders are high-precision, so L0 wash-out (q<=0.6) does not apply. MATH-500 exhibits strong phi<<0 (median -1.0 to -1.2, 86-90% |phi|>0.2, H_C~1.15 vs H_W~2.0, results/phi.csv), confirming the recall-HURTS regime exists in real symbolic-answer data. Stage-B GSM8K null (0.480->0.487, 0.780->0.780, no ranking flip) matches phi~0 prediction and validates the mechanism, providing actionable guidance that integer-answer benchmarks are low-risk. However, the ranking-inversion itself is demonstrated only in L0 simulation (exploratory, post-hoc retune) and remains undemonstrated in-the-wild on real data, limiting operational urgency.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [1] Headline inversion not shown on real models/benchmarks; teams require L2 (MATH with boxed extractor, larger k, two models with differing surface concentration) before changing harnesses. [2] Phi measurement requires real model-sample frequencies; Stage-A phi uses modeled frequencies (proxy), and Stage-B only measured GSM8K (wrong regime). [3] Mechanism is spoiler-effect/Duverger applied to eval (committee#1), not a new mechanism, reducing perceived novelty. [4] Existing harnesses default to exact-match or lexical; switching to numeric canonicalizer needs validation that q=1.0 holds for their answer space.
RATIONALE: Packet cites q=1.0000 with 0 over-merges on 239,881 GSM8K and 4,983 MATH-500 pairs (results/precision_recall.csv). MATH-500 phi<<0 median -0.986 to -1.227 across error regimes, 93-96% |phi|>0.2 (results/phi.csv). Stage-B real-model null on GSM8K (150 problems, k=16, Qwen2.5-0.5B vs 7B) shows 0.480->0.487 and 0.780->0.780, no inversion, consistent with phi~0 (results/stage_b_summary.json). L0 inversion is flagged exploratory with post-hoc retune 0.42/0.46->0.50/0.28 (packet). Residual gaps: phi frequencies proxy, inversion undemonstrated in-the-wild (packet). Prior work: spoiler-effect/Duverger, Bulian2022-BEM, Kuhn2023/Farquhar2024-semantic-entropy, Biderman2024 (packet). Product value is the actionable dataset-specific guidance, but full production hazard requires L2 demonstration.
